  "tagline": "Retired Redis module that ran Cypher over sparse adjacency matrices; succeeded by FalkorDB.",
  "description": "RedisGraph was a Redis module that stored property graphs as sparse adjacency matrices and evaluated Cypher queries with GraphBLAS linear algebra, giving very low latency for in-memory graphs. Redis stopped selling it in July 2023, ended support on 31 January 2025, and the repository README now states it is no longer maintained; the last release was 2.12.10 in October 2023. Its original developers forked it as FalkorDB, which keeps a compatible command model and is the recommended migration path.",
